WEBVTT

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.630
Oh, jeez... Why'd we choose this
cruddy old boat in the first place?!

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.440
I would've stayed at that island's
port if I knew this would happen!

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.440
Even if we wanted to go back,
we couldn't find the port in this fog.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.550
Heaven is punishing
you for stealing it!

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:57.980
Say what?!

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.620
What? What? What? What? What?

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:03.210
First of all, it was YOUR prediction
that got us into this, Filia!

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:04.880
You're really sure it was right?

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:05.950
Of course I am.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.190
Mr. Gourry and Miss Amelia are
on an island to the east of us.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.860
Right, right... What I
really want you to predict...

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:14.560
...is a way for us
to get some cash!

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:18.760
We're out of money because
YOU eat too much, Miss Lina!

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.870
Not having any food is making
me suffer, too, you know!

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.270
What?

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.500
Oh, it's a ship sailing out here.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:02.570
But, I heard tonight is the one night
a year when a ghost ship appears.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:06.210
That's why we couldn't hire
anyone to sail out for us.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.750
Meaning the "ghost ship"
is this thing?

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:15.330
Look, would a ghost ship
be lit up that bright?

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.060
Ghost ships are a lot
more broken down.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.100
And it'd have more
atmosphere, wouldn't it?

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.600
Well, that's true, but...

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.560
Anyway, that ship looks
like it has food on it!

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:24.830
Ray Wing!

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.500
Anyway, let's go.
It may be a ghost ship...

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:30.770
...but I'll take that over
fighting to keep this thing afloat.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:31.870
I suppose so.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:43.920
Hello-o-o! Anybody home?

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.520
You've got a bunch
of strangers on board.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:11.310
Something's very wrong here.
I'm sure of it!

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:19.010
HEY! Anybody home? Hey!

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.520
Wh- What the?

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.200
- Ajar.
- Yeah, a jar.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.600
Welcome aboard!

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.540
I'm Jarlov,
captain of this ship!

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:14.610
Agh! Bad pun alert!

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.970
You mean, this jar is?

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.510
Then this really is the ghost ship?

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:25.460
Oh, I see. You all think
I'm a ghost, is that it?

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:27.680
Anyone would think that.

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:32.130
Well, there are ghosts here.
And evil spirits, too!

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:33.660
Evil spirits?

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:37.840
It was the spirits who
locked me up in this jar.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.600
Locked you up in it?

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:43.270
Anyway, I'm not a ghost and
there are evil spirits here...

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:48.040
...so they call it a ghost ship,
but there aren't any ghosts here.

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:51.410
Seems awfully complicated to me.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:56.720
What's wrong? Hungry?
Then follow me!

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.500
Anyway, Captain, why were
you locked into a jar?

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:09.090
Well, you see...

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:11.470
You did something to get
yourself cursed, didn't you?

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.430
N- No, it wasn't like that.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.740
Look, it doesn't matter to me.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:20.580
Just keep the extra food coming!

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:21.910
You STI LL want to eat MORE?!

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:25.310
Anyway, I feel sorry for
him being in this state.

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:27.720
Could you use your magic
to free him, Miss Lina?

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:28.780
Good question...

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:31.220
What?! You can use magic?!

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.990
If you can, then I beg of you!

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:35.360
Will you help me exorcise the
evil spirits on board here?

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:39.790
Now, look! We're trying to get
to an island to the east of us!

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:42.160
We don't have time to go
busting some evil spirits!

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:43.700
Island to the east?

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.760
I can take you there if you want!
On top of that...

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:47.740
On top of that?

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:52.400
Bust those spirits and set me
free and I'll give you this jar.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.480
I don't want this dirty old jar.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:58.080
What are you saying?!

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.120
This jar is priceless! The only
one of its kind in the world!

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:06.780
They say a king traded all of
his wealth to get this jar!

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.190
All of his wealth?

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:12.720
Now that you mention it, everything
I see here looks like a rare antique.

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:15.360
Oh, this tea
cup is wonderful!

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:19.700
I'm a collector.
You can keep that if you like.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:20.740
You mean it?!

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:23.440
However, you must get
rid of those spirits!

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:26.510
We'll do it for you!
You don't mind, do you, Miss Lina?

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.610
Sure, I'll do it as long as
there's a reward involved.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:30.840
You want anything, Zel?

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.520
Sorry, but I'm not interested.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.680
Looks like the spirits
have begun to move.

00:07:58.280 --> 00:07:59.710
Wh- What's that thing doing?

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:02.340
It pesters me by collecting
all my precious jars.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:05.010
And then night after
night after night, it!

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:06.380
Zel...

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:08.280
Not interested. You handle it.

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:09.340
Jeez...

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:14.850
I can't take it anymore!

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:18.450
Do you know what I went through
to collect those things?!

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:19.660
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:34.510
For crying out loud, are evil
spirits always this violent?!

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.410
Yeah, they are!

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:53.590
Cut it OUT!

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:57.130
What the heck?!

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:04.300
Now what?!

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:08.570
What is this?

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:10.340
A ghost made of jars.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:12.880
It may be big, but it
can't move very fast!

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:14.140
Elmekia...

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:17.110
Those are my jars!
Don't break them!

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.380
...LANCE!

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:20.920
What the?!!

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:27.570
Oh, the color! The sparkle!

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:30.800
It's the lost white magnet jar
with Oldos jade glazed into it!

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:31.960
It's incredibly precious!

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.830
Why don't I use this
chance to take it?

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.780
Agh! My jars!

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:53.390
My jars!

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:56.030
This is all
my fault, isn't it?

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:57.030
Pretty much.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:42.870
Hey! Can't you be more careful?!
What if you break me?!

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:45.340
Sorry!
It was just a little slip.

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:49.750
Anyway, where are
those things hiding?

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.190
Incredible!

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:58.290
Where do you even
begin to choose?!

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.950
They're all rare beauties
I've dreamed of owning!

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:02.590
No wonder he wants
us to be careful!

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:05.150
I have to price these all out!

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:08.290
Where do I start? This one?
Or maybe this one?

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:15.870
The ship's log...

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:34.560
At last, I have it!

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:40.370
The largest, most beautiful,
and most valuable jar in the world.

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:50.720
Polish it more!

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:54.650
Polish it! Polish it!
Make it sparkle in the sun!

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:01.220
Enough of this!
We can't take any more!

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:05.220
Well, what do you want to say?

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:10.470
We don't care about your hobby!
We're not here to polish jars!

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.270
Yeah! He's right!

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:15.670
Captain, which is more important?
Your crew or these jars?

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.530
That's easy. The jars!

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:23.910
Ralmus, don't you understand?
How valuable that jar is?

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:30.090
Making jars... Making jars is
the highest art man practices!

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:34.020
If they're so important to you,
you can polish them yourself!

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:41.130
No, it's my duty as captain
to keep the ship's log.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:50.910
Throw that jar into the sea!

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:51.910
Yeah!

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:55.350
What are you doing?!
Get away from my jar!

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:01.180
Wh- What the devil!

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:06.560
It can't be...
I don't believe this!

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.530
They're getting
ready to come out.

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:37.820
Hey! Don't drop me!

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:39.790
Agh, I can't see! Can't see!

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:43.820
BLAM BLAZER!

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:45.990
What are you aiming at?!
More to the left!

00:13:46.330 --> 00:13:47.930
Blam Blazer!

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:54.000
Sounds like they're
really going at it.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:55.630
Blam Blazer!

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:57.310
Blam Blazer!

00:13:57.510 --> 00:13:59.100
Blam Blazer!

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:03.770
You thought I'd go easy
after you got me this mad?!

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:06.320
H- Hold it!
You're overdoing it!

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.720
Uh, wait!

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:16.960
Ah, I feel much better!

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:20.100
I think I've hired a monster!

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.290
Miss Lina!

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:24.600
Are you all right?!

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:27.600
I think so. Anyway,
what have you got there, Filia?

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:30.170
Oh, would you like to
open it with me, Miss Lina?

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:32.140
My antique shop?

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:34.840
You idiot! You're sure being
laid-back about all this!

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:37.280
Aren't you going to get rid of
those spirits first?!

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:41.780
That's right.
Shall we end this little job?

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.010
Wh- What's?

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:12.280
Why do you interfere with us?
This isn't your concern.

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:15.080
Leave this ship at once!

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:19.020
So, you're the spirits' boss, huh?
YOU guys get off this ship!

00:15:20.130 --> 00:15:22.460
I see there's no
explaining this to you.

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:32.800
We've got another
weird one to deal with...

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:38.540
It's the manifestation of
Ralmus's latent desires.

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:40.980
What do you mean,
"latent desires"?!

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:43.150
Now, take THIS!

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:48.450
I won't lose to
a bunch of mallets!

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:51.950
Come and get me!

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:05.940
YOU I DIOT!!!

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.730
Now what do we do?!

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:34.960
Sorry, I got caught
up in the moment.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:36.300
Would somebody
help me out here?!

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:39.760
You're not
getting away, Captain.

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:41.170
Ralmus!

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:46.180
Captain... Now that these interlopers
are here, we're through playing around.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:48.810
Now our torment will
finally be assuaged!

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:53.480
Mr. Ralmus, wait! I know how
much you hate the captain...

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:56.220
...but it wasn't he
who sank the ship!

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:59.420
Silence!
I don't want to hear that!

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:02.220
Please!
Please forgive the captain!

00:17:02.300 --> 00:17:06.460
I can't. A lot of sailors
died when the ship went down!

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:10.860
Captain, wander forever in
the world of darkness!

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:21.340
Mr. Ralmus!

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:24.180
Filia, this guy isn't
going to listen to you.

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:27.610
So let's send him a nice,
strong example of our concern!

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:32.920
FEL ZA'RED!

00:17:45.140 --> 00:17:46.940
Oh, we're gonna sink...

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:48.370
Captain...

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:49.670
Oh, won't he quit?!

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:53.570
I can't forget them.

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:59.140
My friends who
died in that wreck...

00:17:59.650 --> 00:18:01.140
Ralmus...

00:18:02.320 --> 00:18:06.220
If you hadn't brought
that thing on board...

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:08.330
Filia, what's
he talking about?

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:10.020
I saw the ship's log.

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:12.260
Everything was caused
by the captain's jar.

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:27.840
And that's what
sent the ship down.

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:29.710
You were sunk by an OCTOPUS?!

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:30.770
Ralmus...

00:18:31.990 --> 00:18:34.480
I can't forgive you!

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:39.620
Captain, I'll help Ralmus's soul
pass on to the next world.

00:18:39.690 --> 00:18:40.790
Can you do that?

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:46.600
Yes. All of you,
pray with me.

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:55.440
Holy... Rezast...

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:01.780
Oh, thank you!

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:09.850
Oh, boy... Can I assume
the case is closed now?

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:16.420
Oh! At last,
I can pass on as well!

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:20.000
I know I said I was
locked in the jar...

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:22.370
...but the truth is that
I was a ghost as well.

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:23.400
Well, duh!

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:27.070
Anyone could have figured that
out with a moment of thought.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:31.510
Anyway, I couldn't pass on
while I was trapped in there.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.340
Now that I know how Ralmus
and the others felt...

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:37.350
...I no longer
want to collect jars.

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:40.480
Well, if you can pass on,
no point in waiting around here.

00:19:40.550 --> 00:19:44.420
I was hoping to build up the
emotional level here, you know.

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:47.160
Hey, don't take
it personally!

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:49.920
We don't want HI M
turning into a vengeful spirit.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:53.490
Still, you both have
done me a great service.

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:54.970
I thank you.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.010
Oh, well.

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:32.300
I can barely believe what
we went through last night.

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:34.670
And our reward ended up
on the bottom of the sea.

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:35.770
Oh, look!

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:38.770
I managed to
save one of them!

00:20:38.850 --> 00:20:40.310
When did you do that?

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:50.520
Typical ghost ship...
Hold it! That means!

00:20:50.590 --> 00:20:52.790
All that food we
ate last night!

00:20:56.760 --> 00:21:02.760
I HATE ghost ships!
Ugh! Gross!

00:22:22.280 --> 00:22:25.080
Gourry! Amelia!
Where are you hiding now?!

00:22:25.150 --> 00:22:27.950
If you don't come out, you
can't get any more screen time!

00:22:28.020 --> 00:22:30.960
Next time, " Immediate Results?
Love is in the Tiny Differences!"

00:22:31.020 --> 00:22:33.650
You'd better watch, or I'll
REALLY cause some trouble!
